LICENCE HISTORY
===============

OmniHub was released under the MIT licence through version 1.3.3 and was
relicensed to GPL-3.0 during the 1.5 development cycle.

The relicence was possible because the repository has a single copyright
holder; `git log` shows no other author. It was done so that the project could
draw on the existing body of open-source laptop fan control work, effectively
all of which is copyleft, rather than re-deriving hardware interfaces other
people have already measured and published.

Anyone who obtained OmniHub under the MIT licence keeps MIT rights to that
code. This change binds what happens from here on, not what was already given
away.


THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS SHIPPED WITH THIS PROGRAM
================================================

PawnIO modules
  namazso/PawnIO.Modules -- https://github.com/namazso/PawnIO.Modules
  LGPL-2.1-or-later.

  Signed bytecode modules distributed under OmniHub.App/Assets/PawnIO/. They
  are loaded by, not linked into, this program: the PawnIO driver executes them
  in its own sandbox and OmniHub reaches them only through named ioctls. They
  are redistributed unmodified, and their licence notice is kept with them.

  The PawnIO driver itself is installed separately, from its own publisher, and
  is not distributed here.


SOURCES THIS PROGRAM DRAWS ON
